'You're mean!' No, I'm not mean. It's an animal, people!

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.669
We have to keep our brains plugged in.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:44.819
See, the problem is my wife grew up on a farm, and animals left every week and went somewhere called "bye-bye".

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:52.799
And, um, like Jeff Foxworthy said, he said, 'we had a cat that tore up our--my mom's curtains and the next day that cat "ran away".' (laughter)

00:01:57.759 --> 00:02:03.029
Yeah, so Sharon grew up on the farm, and these animals were always "running away".

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:09.750
And we just understand that they're animals. We love them. We have a heart, we're not mean,

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.880
